#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0085.1 expect=violation domain=BW
#note "THE CELL THE DEFECT CONTROLLED (Fix #285 / M3-D2). Row 1 has an empty --ORRES and an empty --STAT: with the literal double-quoted, `\"\" != \"NOT DONE\"` is TRUE (ScalarSemantics.equalsNumericAware folds a missing left operand to the empty string and compares as text) and the row FIRES. Before M3-D2 the second disjunct carried var_exists(`NOT DONE`), which is false everywhere, so that whole arm collapsed and only the '--STAT column absent' arm survived -- the rule UNDER-reported its central population (note: the batch record's 'OVER-REPORTS' label is wrong; the analysis under it is right). Row 2 is legitimately not done and row 3 carries a result, so both are silent under either reading; the fixture isolates exactly the one cell."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 BWSEQ=1
dataset BW class=FINDINGS label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col BWTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col BWORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
col BWSTAT   type=Char label="Completion Status"
---
S1 | BW | 001 | 1 | BW |     |
S1 | BW | 001 | 2 | BW |     | NOT DONE
S1 | BW | 001 | 3 | BW | 250 |
---
